{"availability":"available","full":"vfydr2m9wk-ops/InkDOS","name":"InkDOS","description":"A lightweight local-first productivity suite for focused DOCX, XLS/XLSX, and PPTX workflows.","category":"Productivity","language":"Python","stars":15,"forks":1,"created":"2026-08-03T19:17:19Z","updated":"2026-10-08T22:07:50Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://vfydr2m9wk-ops.github.io/InkDOS/","topics":[],"demo":"https://vfydr2m9wk-ops.github.io/InkDOS/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.219Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.219Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.219Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:54:49.285Z","stars":15,"forks":1},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:49.219Z","stars":15,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["InkDOS is a personal, local-first office hub: one Home that opens documents, spreadsheets, presentations, PDFs, e-books and plain text, entirely in the browser or in a small Windows app. There is no account, no server and no telemetry. Files are opened from the device and saved back to it.","I wanted one place to open and edit my files on every device I actually use (an iPad, often inside the XeOS web desktop, iPad Safari, and a Windows PC) without installing a full office suite on each one, without uploading documents anywhere, and without a heavy app eating RAM. Office suites in the browser usually mean a cloud account; desktop suites mean a large install per device. InkDOS sits in between: a static web app that works offline once loaded, and the same thing packaged for Windows.","It began as a set of lightweight editors written for this project. Over time the goal changed: instead of rebuilding what mature open-source projects already do well, InkDOS now gathers them behind one Home and keeps them on the device."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vfydr2m9wk-ops/InkDOS/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3ef091725758cbfcb29cc6876a86d0